# The human review surface. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.
#
# Every pull request into main needs an approval, so this file does not decide
# whether a person looks at a change. It decides which person, and on a
# milestone/** branch, where no approval is required, it is the whole rule:
# an owned path in the diff is what pulls a reviewer in, and everything else
# merges unattended behind the gates in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# Four paths, each here for its own reason:
#
#   e2e/                  the requirements themselves, stated as executable
#                         specs. An agent that may edit these can make a
#                         failing requirement pass by rewriting it.
#   packages/db/drizzle/  applied migrations: the one change a later fix
#                         cannot undo.
#   .github/              the gates, and this file. Both are what make
#                         everything above enforceable rather than stated.
#   stryker.config.ts     the coverage floor. Its `!` lines take files out of
#                         the only gate that requires them to be tested, so a
#                         test that got hard to write has a one-line way out
#                         that nothing else would review. ADR-0004.

/e2e/                      @kinchi22
/packages/db/drizzle/      @kinchi22
/.github/                  @kinchi22
/stryker.config.ts         @kinchi22
